{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>On the very day.</b> And not delaying to do the thing, and behold there were three hundred and eighteen homeborn of his household besides those bought with his money, and afterward Abraham was circumcised also on the same day, and Ishmael his son and the homeborn of his household and those bought with his money — all were circumcised with him willingly, and the reason is that he did not coerce them, but they all hastened to do and to fulfill the will of HaShem:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:53.045992759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}